<title>USA: ACT buys Irish company, plans new plant.</title>
<headline>ACT buys Irish company, plans new plant.</headline>
<dateline>HUDSON, Mass. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>ACT Manufacturing Inc said Tuesday it acquired Signmax Ltd, a Dublin, Ireland-based cable and harness contract manufacturer.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed. In a statement, ACT said Signmax currently has annual sales of about $5 million.</p>
<p>In the same statement, ACT also said it plans to begin constructing a new manufacturing facility in Ireland for printed circuit board and assembly operations.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to provide further information about its construction plans.</p>
</text>
